Description
The
Boyer-Moore
type algorithms match some suffixes of the pattern but it is possible to match some prefixes of the pattern by scanning the character of the window from right to left and then improve the length of the shifts. This is made possible by the use of the smallest suffix automaton (also called DAWG for Directed Acyclic Word Graph) of the reverse pattern. The resulting algorithm is called the Reverse Factor algorithm.
